fhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f362b3931ba54ab8ea7346551143e7790c52fcc8189a887083ce71aa231746ce","event_uuid":"65eead66-2bac-485a-8344-a5e12f704a50","position":{"commit_sha":"6f522176901cb0335105c5c8f61fbfab3b3203da","position":"1788907758154164001-65eead66-2bac-485a-8344-a5e12f704a50"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fresh orphan sweep triage 2026-09-08: parentless non-epic newly filed since the TSV, but not executable in this sweep. The ticket explicitly requires /rebar-debug-style controlled idle/concurrent-load experiments for a fresh temporary-store git subprocess timeout, and relates to closed bd66 as a recurrence class requiring separate investigation. Disposition: keep open for a dedicated debugging owner; do not claim here because the next action is RCA experimentation, not a bounded code fix.","timestamp":1788905080815253001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA progress 2026-09-08: Observation reproduced under controlled idle conditions in this worktree with TMPDIR routed to .rebar/tmp (no shared /tmp scratch): tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass passed but took 268.13s, only ~32s below the repo-wide pytest-timeout 300s budget. Hypothesis H1: the fresh-store stall is not a malformed store or Gerrit/network dependency; it is deterministic per-event write publishability probing inside the batched importer. Experiment 1 (single variable: monkeypatch write_blocking_divergence to no-op for the same import shape): 50 CREATE+COMMENT records took 5.099s with the real probe versus 0.666s with only that probe removed; the real probe consumed 4.44s. Experiment 2 (single variable: count git calls while keeping behavior real): 10 CREATE+COMMENT records made 41 `git remote get-url origin` calls and 20 `git rev-parse --verify origin/tickets` calls, i.e. the supposedly batched import still pays two remote-url probes and one remote-ref probe per event before the batched commit. Idle 3000-record runtime scales from this per-event cost, so modest concurrent validation load pushes the benchmark over 300s and the timeout stack lands wherever the current git child is blocked (observed at `remote get-url origin`). H1 currently confirmed; next fix should preserve the write-divergence safety check but run it once per batch flush, not once per buffered event.","timestamp":1788906266774547001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"TDD RED recorded: added tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_import_checks_publishability_once_per_batch_commit as the deterministic oracle. On unmodified code it failed: importing 10 tickets with one comment each made 20 write-publishability checks (one per buffered CREATE and COMMENT event) instead of the intended 2 checks (one before the CREATE batch commit and one before the COMMENT batch commit). This confirms the root cause at the batching seam before applying the fix.","timestamp":1788907758154164001}],"created_at":1788902638223483001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ce6566f3-7186-45fc-b243-119a15abf26d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"717a-ebd1-42f0-4dec"},{"link_uuid":"d97fad8f-f7f3-46f0-9ed6-d36e95429733","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bd66-28a4-fd31-4c9f"}],"description":"## Context\nWhile validating documentation-only leaf 717a-ebd1-42f0-4dec at exact commit d12389b8d840dee4c10ddd48e7e1801aad7373ee, the focused interface suite timed out in test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass. The stack was blocked in subprocess.run for git -C <fresh repo> remote get-url origin, called by write_blocking_divergence during import_tickets. This ran concurrently with other bounded local validation. Closed bug bd66-28a4-fd31-4c9f explicitly says a recurrence on a fresh store needs a separate investigation; its mature-store foreground-maintenance fix does not explain this fresh-store occurrence.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce under controlled idle and concurrent-load conditions in an isolated worktree.\n- Capture the exact git child argv, duration, process state, and host load at the stall.\n- Distinguish scheduler or I/O starvation, inherited git configuration or hooks, credential-helper behavior, and a fixture or store-path defect with one-variable experiments.\n- Fix the proven failure class and add a deterministic regression oracle without weakening time bounds.\n\n## Testing\n- RED: `pytest tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::<new lowcost regression>` must fail before the fix by showing batched import still calls write_blocking_divergence per buffered event.\n- GREEN targeted: `pytest tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::<new lowcost regression> tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py::test_benchmark_commit_count_is_ceil_per_pass tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py`.\n- Final verification: `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=8` with ambient GIT_CONFIG_* variables unset.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The timeout mechanism is reproduced or falsified with recorded evidence.\n- [ ] Competing hypotheses receive discriminating experiments and verdicts.\n- [ ] Any fix targets the proven class and has RED-before-GREEN regression coverage.\n- [ ] The affected focused interface suite passes reliably under its supported concurrency envelope.\n- [ ] Findings and residual risks are recorded on this ticket.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py","reason":"Batch-sink write path should defer the publishability probe for buffered events while preserving direct-write behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py","reason":"Flush each import batch only after one publishability probe, preserving split-history refusal without per-event git probes."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/io/test_import_batch_resume.py","reason":"Regression coverage proving batched import does not run the write-divergence probe per imported event and still probes before each batch commit."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","bd66-28a4-fd31-4c9f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4073e6e6-abe4-4fef-accb-0e441b2c628d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["test-reliability","git","store","debug"],"ticket_id":"0c8f-1728-6cc9-4c17","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Diagnose fresh temporary-store git subprocess timeout under concurrent validation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["52bd5da0-8415-42bd-b7b4-27cc94bdce8c","ce6566f3-7186-45fc-b243-119a15abf26d","d97fad8f-f7f3-46f0-9ed6-d36e95429733","5ac42111-44b9-497b-92db-041bc848309e","f5cedfd6-ba60-4949-ad4d-7e7e5fcf7f52","7c3e91d8-a5ea-407f-b584-31939349991f","19f42e8b-3e9c-42a3-91bd-edaee6b248dd","b24a3922-2d48-4654-98d6-1d1f5f45e4c4","4073e6e6-abe4-4fef-accb-0e441b2c628d","1e28f3cb-d2c2-43c0-a37c-faa38d71ee03","65eead66-2bac-485a-8344-a5e12f704a50"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788912463467298001,"uuid":"848b25e9-9e0b-4511-9934-acf30522b49a"}